  "notes": "{乱|みだ}す is a transitive godan verb meaning to throw into disorder, to disturb, or to disrupt.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {乱|みだ}れる (intransitive — to become disordered)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{乱|みだ}している means 'is disrupting' (ongoing action).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {秩序|ちつじょ}を{乱|みだ}す: to disturb order\n- {風紀|ふうき}を{乱|みだ}す: to corrupt public morals\n- {平和|へいわ}を{乱|みだ}す: to disturb the peace\n- {心|こころ}を{乱|みだ}す: to upset one's composure\n- {列|れつ}を{乱|みだ}す: to break ranks/formation\n- {髪|かみ}を{乱|みだ}す: to dishevel one's hair\n\nREGISTER:\nSomewhat formal. Common in news, rules, and literary contexts. In everyday speech, ぐちゃぐちゃにする (to mess up) or {崩|くず}す (to break down) are more casual alternatives.",
